    "result": "I wrote `EnableFeature` in `feature.go` and added tests in `feature_test.go`, but I have not run them. The environment blocked `go test`, so run `go test ./...` yourself.\n\nHow it handles repeat runs and crashes:\n- **Running twice:** it reads the current file and compares the text. If the feature line already says `on`, it writes nothing.\n- **Crash during a write:** it writes to a temp file and then renames it over the config. A crash leaves the old file or the new one, never a half-written file.\n- **Leftover temp files:** a crashed run can leave a `.\u003cname\u003e.tmp-*` file behind. A later run deletes it once it is over 1 hour old.\n- **Existing lines:** other lines stay exactly as they were, including CRLF line endings. If the feature line is there with another value, it changes in place to `on`. Duplicate lines for the same feature are merged into one.\n\nI did not add a lock. If two runs write *different* keys to the same file at the same moment, one can overwrite the other's change. A retried deploy that sets the same feature is safe, since both runs write the same result.",
